// lexdb over TDS: the audit's wrong answers and wrong errors in the T-SQL door, checked against SQL Server 2025 (generated by
// tests/lexdb/gen_mssql.py --port 14331 --container lxl-mssql25 newfix from mssql_newfix_queries.txt; design/lexdb-new-features.md):
// GROUP BY ALL (the groups WHERE removed, their aggregates over no rows; with HAVING, ORDER BY, joins, 3,000 rows), a select alias
// (207) or a constant (164) in GROUP BY, GENERATE_SERIES's column value, || of two numbers (402), SUBSTRING and FORMAT of a NULL
// constant (8116), FORMAT's .NET format strings, DATEADD of a string (a datetime), an unknown function refused when the batch is
// compiled (195, an empty input too), IS DISTINCT FROM as a value (156), CHAR and NCHAR. Each batch runs against lexdb with SET
// lexdb_batch = off and on: "same: " and the answer, or DIFFERENT and both.
// expect: ok
// expect: (5)
// expect: ok
// expect: (3000)
// expect: same: a,n,s: NULL|0|NULL;1|1|20;2|1|30;3|0|NULL
// expect: same: a,n,m,mt: NULL|0|NULL|NULL;1|0|NULL|NULL;2|0|NULL|NULL;3|0|NULL|NULL
// expect: same: a,n: NULL|0;1|0;2|0;3|0
